      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אֲבַדּוֹן</span></big>  <strong>subst. fem.</strong><sup>?</sup> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.20\">Pr 27:20</a> abstrato, praticamente equivalente a <strong>nome próprio</strong> (lugar de) <strong>Destruição, Ruína</strong>, <strong>ʾAbaddôn (</strong>cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܰܒܕܳܢܳܐ</span> 𝔊 <a data-ref=\"Job 28:22\" href=\"/Job.28.22\">Jb 28:22</a> etc.<strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">אֲבַדּוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 26:6\" href=\"/Job.26.6\">Jb 26:6</a> (+ 4 ocorrências); abreviatura: <span dir=\"rtl\">אבדה</span> Kt <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲבַדּוֹ(ן)</span> Qr †<a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.20\">Pr 27:20</a>.—Lugar de ruína no Sh<sup>e</sup>ʾôl, para os mortos perdidos ou arruinados, como desenvolvimento de uma distinção anterior de condição no Sh<sup>e</sup>ʾôl (ver <a data-ref=\"BDB, שְׁאוֹל\" href=\"/BDB,_שְׁאוֹל\" dir=\"rtl\">שְׁאוֹל</a>). Somente na literatura sapiencial (WisdLt); <a data-ref=\"Job 31:12\" href=\"/Job.31.12\">Jb 31:12</a>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁאול</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 26:6\" href=\"/Job.26.6\">Jb 26:6</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 15:11\" href=\"/Proverbs.15.11\">Pr 15:11</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:20\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.20\">27:20</a>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מות</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 28:22\" href=\"/Job.28.22\">Jb 28:22</a>; ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">קבר</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 88:12\" href=\"/Psalms.88.12\">ψ 88:12</a>.",
