      "preview": "Verbo: estar disposto, consentir; formas do Qal e usos positivos e negativos.",
      "html": "† I. <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">אָבָה</span></big></big>  <strong>verbo: estar disposto, consentir (</strong>cf. assírio <em>abîtu</em>, <em>desejar</em>, Dl<sup>W</sup>, etiópico አበየ: <em>recusar</em>, árabe <span dir=\"rtl\">أَبَى</span>, <em>idem</em>, no dialeto de Najd, <em>estar disposto</em> So<sup>De Jes 3, p. 26; LCB 1880, 817</sup><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>Qal</strong> (com <span dir=\"rtl\">לֹא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַל</span> exceto em <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:19\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.19\">Is 1:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 39:9\" href=\"/Job.39.9\">Jb 39:9</a>; no Hexateuco, raro e somente em JED, inclusive <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:21\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.21\">Lv 26:21</a>); perfeito: <span dir=\"rtl\">אָבָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 10:27\" href=\"/Exodus.10.27\">Ex 10:27</a> + <span dir=\"rtl\">אָבוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:25\" href=\"/Judges.19.25\">Ju 19:25</a> + 7 ocorrências; <span dir=\"rtl\">אָבוּא</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 28:12\" href=\"/Isaiah.28.12\">Is 28:12</a> (Sta<sup>§ 31 R. 2</sup>; Kö<sup>I, 414</sup>); imperfeito: <span dir=\"rtl\">יֹאבֶה</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 29:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.29.19\">Dt 29:19</a> + 2 ocorrências; 2.ª pessoa masc. sing., jussivo: <span dir=\"rtl\">תֹּבֵא</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:10\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.10\">Pr 1:10</a> (Sta<sup>§ 143 e 1 fin</sup>; Kö<sup>I, 576 f</sup>) etc.; particípio: <span dir=\"rtl\">אֹבִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.7\">Ez 3:7</a>;—<em>estar disposto</em>, seguido de infinitivo com ל <a data-ref=\"Exodus 10:27\" href=\"/Exodus.10.27\">Ex 10:27</a> + 29 ocorrências; sem ל <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:30\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.30\">Dt 2:30</a> + 8 ocorrências; sujeito: <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 10:10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.10.10\">Dt 10:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 23:6\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.23.6\">23:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 29:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.29.19\">29:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 24:10\" href=\"/Joshua.24.10\">Jos 24:10</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 8:19\" href=\"/II_Kings.8.19\">2 K 8:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 13:23\" href=\"/II_Kings.13.23\">13:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Kings 24:4\" href=\"/II_Kings.24.4\">24:4</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 21:7\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.21.7\">2 Ch 21:7</a>; sujeito humano: <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:5\" href=\"/Genesis.24.5\">Gn 24:5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 24:8\" href=\"/Genesis.24.8\">8</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:10\" href=\"/Judges.19.10\">Ju 19:10</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:21\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.21\">2 S 2:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:25\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.25\">13:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 14:29\" href=\"/II_Samuel.14.29\">14:29</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:16\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.16\">23:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:17\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.17\">17</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:18\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.18\">1 Ch 11:18</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:19\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.19\">19</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 19:19\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.19.19\">1 Ch 19:19</a>; em sentido negativo: <a data-ref=\"Exodus 10:27\" href=\"/Exodus.10.27\">Ex 10:27</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 2:30\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.2.30\">Dt 2:30</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.7\">25:7</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:25\" href=\"/Judges.19.25\">Ju. 19:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:13\" href=\"/Judges.20.13\">20:13</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:14\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.14\">2 S 13:14</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:16\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.16\">16</a>; especialmente de Israel obstinado: <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 26:21\" href=\"/Leviticus.26.21\">Lv 26:21</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 1:26\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.1.26\">Dt 1:26</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 15:9\" href=\"/I_Samuel.15.9\">1 S 15:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 28:12\" href=\"/Isaiah.28.12\">Is 28:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 30:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.30.9\">30:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 42:24\" href=\"/Isaiah.42.24\">42:24</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 3:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.3.7\">Ez 3:7</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 20:8\" href=\"/Ezekiel.20.8\">20:8</a>; sujeito animal: <span dir=\"rtl\">רֵים</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 39:9\" href=\"/Job.39.9\">Jb 39:9</a>; em uso absoluto (sem infinitivo): <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 12:17\" href=\"/II_Samuel.12.17\">2 S 12:17</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 20:8\" href=\"/I_Kings.20.8\">1 K 20:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 22:50\" href=\"/I_Kings.22.50\">22:50</a>; cf. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:35\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.35\">Pr 6:35</a>, referindo-se a homem ciumento; em sentido negativo: <a data-ref=\"Judges 11:17\" href=\"/Judges.11.17\">Ju 11:17</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 30:15\" href=\"/Isaiah.30.15\">Is 30:15</a>; em sentido positivo: <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 22:17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.22.17\">1 S 22:17</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 26:23\" href=\"/I_Samuel.26.23\">26:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 31:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.31.4\">31:4</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 10:4\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.10.4\">1 Ch 10:4</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 6:10\" href=\"/II_Samuel.6.10\">2 S 6:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:10\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.10\">Pr 1:10</a>; seguido de verbo finito: <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:19\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.19\">Is 1:19</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(אִם תֹּאבוּ וּשְׁמַעְתֶּם)</span> <em>consentir, ceder a</em>, seguido de <span dir=\"rtl\">לוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 13:9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.13.9\">Dt 13:9</a> (sentido positivo); seguido de <span dir=\"rtl\">לִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:12\" href=\"/Psalms.81.12\">ψ 81:12</a>; seguido de <span dir=\"rtl\">לַעֲצָתִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:30\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.30\">Pr 1:30</a>; seguido de acusativo: <span dir=\"rtl\">תּוֹכַחְתִּי</span> versículo <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:25\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.25\">25</a> (todos em sentido negativo).",
